  18	/// Sort key for a `Version` field inside a hand-written `Ord` impl.
  19	///
  20	/// `(grammar, raw)` is exactly the subset of `Version`'s own derived
  21	/// `PartialEq`/`Eq` fields needed to keep a containing type's `Ord`
  22	/// consistent with its `Eq`: `parsed` is a pure function of `(grammar,
  23	/// raw)` (see `Version::parse`), so it draws no further distinctions once
  24	/// grammar and raw already agree. `render()` (== `raw`) alone is NOT
  25	/// enough -- the same literal string parses under more than one grammar
  26	/// (e.g. `"1.2.3"` is valid SemVer *and* PEP 440), so two `Version`s with
  27	/// different `grammar` but identical `render()` output would compare
  28	/// unequal via derived `Eq` yet `Ordering::Equal` via a `render()`-only
  29	/// `Ord`, violating the invariant `BTreeSet`/`BTreeMap` require:
  30	/// `a.cmp(b) == Equal` iff `a == b`.
  31	fn version_ord_key(v: &Version) -> (VersionGrammar, &str) {
  32	    (v.grammar(), v.render())
  33	}
